{"basis": "Supplied first-assessment-2027 guide and supplied website HTML, reviewed 17 November 2026.", "scope": "Structural inventory of every official topic and numbered understanding, plus targeted substantive content and rendering review. This is not certification that every requirement is fully taught or assessed.", "summary": {"officialTopics": 24, "officialUnderstandings": 161, "topicsRepresentedInOriginal": 24, "whollyMissingTopics": 0, "standaloneHtmlDocuments": 26, "duplicateTopicDocuments": 1, "additionalQuizDocuments": 1, "slTopics": 13, "hlOnlyTopics": 11}, "findings": [{"id": "structure", "severity": "structural", "topics": [], "finding": "The supplied file concatenates 26 standalone HTML documents. There are 24 distinct official topic lessons, a duplicate A2.1 lesson and an additional Young’s Modulus quiz.", "resolution": "Use one consistent application shell; keep one A2.1 lesson and retain the additional quiz."}, {"id": "codes", "severity": "navigation", "topics": ["B4.1", "C4.1"], "finding": "Production systems and Design for manufacture titles are labelled only 4.1. The A3.2 title also spaces A 3.2 inconsistently.", "resolution": "Use the official A/B/C topic prefixes in every curriculum location."}, {"id": "electronics-units", "severity": "content", "topics": ["A3.4"], "statements": ["A3.4.4"], "finding": "The SI multiplier series p, n, μ, m, k, M, G, T is not explicitly taught. Quantities and symbols are only partly developed.", "resolution": "Add a prefix conversion reference and worked conversion challenge."}, {"id": "electronics-symbols", "severity": "depth", "topics": ["A3.4", "B3.4"], "statements": ["A3.4.14", "B3.4.6"], "finding": "Circuit-symbol recognition and circuit construction are described in prose, with no displayed component-symbol set or circuit construction workspace in these lessons.", "resolution": "Provide an accessible visual symbol reference and practical drawing task."}, {"id": "logic-depth", "severity": "content", "topics": ["B3.4"], "statements": ["B3.4.9"], "finding": "AND/OR/NOT output values are listed, but explicit Boolean notation and sequential logic with memory are not explained; learners are not asked to construct a full interactive truth table.", "resolution": "Add Boolean notation, combinational versus sequential explanation, and gated truth-table practice."}, {"id": "broken-exam", "severity": "critical", "topics": ["B3.4"], "statements": ["B3.4.3", "B3.4.4"], "finding": "Q2 has missing resistor values and blank choices; Q3 has missing LED voltage/current/supply data; Q4 omits pump voltage. Several teaching equations are empty. The HTML itself lacks these values, so this is not merely a rendering issue.", "resolution": "Retain the question intentions but rebuild them as clearly labelled repaired questions with stated numbers and worked solutions."}, {"id": "citation-artifacts", "severity": "quality", "topics": ["B3.4"], "finding": "Literal [cite: 1] tokens appear throughout electronics teaching and questions without a resolvable source.", "resolution": "Remove broken tokens and distinguish model classroom examples from verified commercial claims."}, {"id": "duration", "severity": "accuracy", "topics": ["A3.4", "B3.4", "C3.2"], "finding": "Lesson durations differ from the guide: A3.4 says approximately 4–5 hours (guide: 6); B3.4 says 16 hours (guide: 10); C3.2 says 3 hours (guide: 7).", "resolution": "Display the guide’s topic hours consistently; distinguish suggested activity timings."}, {"id": "lca-depth", "severity": "depth", "topics": ["C3.2"], "statements": ["C3.2.1", "C3.2.2"], "finding": "LCA has an overview, stage table and questions but limited quantitative inventory comparison and impact-category interpretation. It is among the shortest lessons despite a 7-hour allocation. Word count is a signal, not proof of insufficiency.", "resolution": "Add explicit material/energy inventory practice and multi-category trade-off evaluation."}, {"id": "glossary", "severity": "coverage", "topics": ["C2.1"], "finding": "C2.1 contains no dedicated glossary section; the other 23 topic lessons have glossary sections, but full term completeness against the supplied glossary is not implied.", "resolution": "Populate every topic from the supplied official topic-specific glossary."}, {"id": "feedback", "severity": "accuracy", "topics": ["A3.4"], "statements": ["A3.4.11"], "finding": "The hand-dryer example treats rechecking hand presence as output feedback. Presence is an input; output feedback needs measurement of a controlled output quantity.", "resolution": "Use a thermostat measuring achieved temperature as the unambiguous closed-loop example."}, {"id": "lca-claim", "severity": "quality", "topics": ["C3.2"], "finding": "The lesson presents 12,274 litres of water per cotton T-shirt without an attributable source or boundary conditions.", "resolution": "Remove this unsupported universal figure; use explicitly fictional classroom inventory data."}], "topics": [{"code": "A1.1", "title": "Ergonomics", "level": "SL/HL", "officialHours": 10, "originalTopicPresent": true, "understandingCount": 7, "originalWordCount": 3444, "images": 0, "videoEmbeds": 0, "findingIds": [], "statementReview": [{"code": "A1.1.1", "status": "mapped; detailed mastery not certified"}, {"code": "A1.1.2", "status": "mapped; detailed mastery not certified"}, {"code": "A1.1.3", "status": "mapped; detailed mastery not certified"}, {"code": "A1.1.4", "status": "mapped; detailed mastery not certified"}, {"code": "A1.1.5", "status": "mapped; detailed mastery not certified"}, {"code": "A1.1.6", "status": "mapped; detailed mastery not certified"}, {"code": "A1.1.7", "status": "mapped; detailed mastery not certified"}]}, {"code": "A2.1", "title": "User-centred research methods", "level": "SL/HL", "officialHours": 5, "originalTopicPresent": true, "understandingCount": 5, "originalWordCount": 5257, "images": 0, "videoEmbeds": 2, "findingIds": [], "statementReview": [{"code": "A2.1.1", "